  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe issue https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10677 proposed adding `TextMetrics.getTextClusters()` to retrieve text grapheme clusters. This will  achieve cluster isolation.  It also proposed adding `CanvasRenderingContext2D.fillTextCluster()` to be able to display the text cluster by cluster.\n\nBut the problem is `fillTextCluster()` has to take the same x and y for all the clusters, which getTextClusters() returned, if they need to be displayed contiguous. If any change in the position is needed, this has to be applied as a transform to the `CanvasRenderingContext2D` before calling `fillTextCluster()`.\n\nThis is confusing and limiting at the same time.  A cluster has to retain all the information that is needed to display it correctly. It can hold the glyphs, the advances and reference its font. But where this cluster is displayed relative to the rest of the clusters should not be considered a correctness issue. Implementing sub-script and super-script will be hard using this model.",
